# Testing and gates

## Automated Proof

Nothing is "done" until its tests exist and pass. Tests must be **behavioural** — if a test's
failure would not indicate a user-visible defect, it is the wrong test. Coverage that asserts
implementation detail is worse than no coverage.

```bash
npm run verify      # typecheck + lint + boundaries + test + build   ← the gate
npm run coverage    # thresholds enforced
npm run bench       # budgets, fails on >10% regression
npm run e2e         # Playwright (from Phase 1)
```

## Coverage thresholds — ratcheted, never lowered

| Path | Stmts | Branch | Funcs |
|---|---|---|---|
| `src/engine/**`, `src/shared/**` | **95%** | **90%** | **95%** |
| `src/render/**`, `src/server/**` | 85% | 75% | 85% |
| `src/ui/**`, `src/themes/**` | 70% | 60% | 70% |

A phase that would lower a threshold must instead delete or fix the untested code.

## Performance budgets (CI-gated, 10% tolerance)

| Metric | Phase 0 floor | Phase 5 target |
|---|---|---|
| Conway steps/sec @ 512² soup | ≥ 60 | ≥ 400 |
| Conway steps/sec @ 4096² @1% | ≥ 5 | ≥ 60 |
| Frame time, 1080p steady state | ≤ 16.6 ms | ≤ 8 ms |
| Main-thread block per tick | ≤ 4 ms | ≤ 1 ms |
| Cold interactive load | ≤ 1500 ms | ≤ 800 ms |
| Client JS bundle (gzip) | ≤ 120 kB | ≤ 180 kB |

Benchmarks take the median of N runs against a committed `bench-baseline.json`. Updating the
baseline is a reviewed commit, never a reflex.

## Other standing gates

- **Boundary checker** — zero violations, with fixtures proving it *catches* violations.
- **Determinism** — identical snapshots at tick 5,000 across instances and across builds.
- **Allocation** — < 1 MB heap growth over 1,000 steps in steady state.
- **Playwright E2E** (Phase 1+) — green on Chromium, Firefox and WebKit; non-flaky over 10 runs.
- **Visual regression** (Phase 1+, per-theme from Phase 3) — 48 baselines, ≤ 0.1% pixel tolerance.
- **axe-core** — zero violations, in every theme from Phase 3.
- **Dashboard freshness** — `node .agents/scripts/build-dashboard.mjs --check`.

**Never weaken a gate to make a build pass.** Fix the code, or escalate.
